    "updated_at": "2025-05-20T14:03:06Z",
    "body": "So the proposal here is to use https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-secure-contexts/#is-url-trustworthy on request's current URL instead of doing a scheme check? That's probably reasonable, but does seem best tackled as follow-up. (This does make me recall we never quite fully settled how Secure Contexts and HTML integrate, but that isn't really a blocker.)\n\nThe initial PR was doing a secure context check on request's client, which is quite a bit different.",
